REGENT OF DONGGALA

CENTRAL SULAWESI PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF DONGGALA REGENCY

NUMBER 5 OF 2014

CONCERNING

PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF DONGGALA,

a. that women and children are creations of Almighty God who constitute important elements of Indonesian society and nation;

b. that Indonesian women have an important role in community activities, development and family life and have the obligation to nurture, protect and raise Indonesian children to grow and develop as the nation's future generation;

c. that Indonesian children are Indonesian human resources who will later become actors in all fields of social and state life;
d. that in social life, women and children in Donggala Regency often experience violence or unpleasant treatment so it is considered important to protect them;
e. based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d, a Regional Regulation of Donggala Regency concerning Protection for Women and Children is established.

Considering: 1. 6.

Law Number 29 of 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi Donggala (State Gazette of 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);

Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3143);

Law Number 6 of 1974 concerning Basic Provisions of Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1974 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3039);

Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);

Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3668);

Law Number 20 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 138 concerning Minimum Age for Admission to Employment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 56, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3835);

Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3941);

